","summary":"One who follows on another’s heels; supplanter, (Gen. 25:26; 27:36; Hos. 12:2-4), the second born of the twin sons of Isaac by Rebekah. He was born probably at Lahai-roi, when his father was fifty-nine and Abraham one hundred and fifty-nine years old.","verses":1009,"father":"Isaac","mother":"Rebekah","v":[1,4,10,28]},{"id":"moses_2108","name":"Moses","also":"","summary":"Drawn (or Egypt. mesu, “son;” hence Rameses, royal son). On the invitation of Pharaoh (Gen. 45:17-25), Jacob and his sons went down into Egypt.","verses":774,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[1,4]},{"id":"reuben_2429","name":"Reuben","also":"","summary":"Behold a son!, the eldest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 29:32). His sinful conduct, referred to in Gen. 35:22, brought down upon him his dying father’s malediction (48:4).","verses":70,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[6]},{"id":"judah_1751","name":"Judah","also":"","summary":"Praise, the fourth son of Jacob by Leah.","verses":245,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[7]},{"id":"levi_1820","name":"Levi","also":"","summary":"The third son of Jacob by Leah. The origin of the name is found in Leah’s words (Gen. 29:34), “This time will my husband be joined [Heb. yillaveh] unto me.”","verses":64,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[8]},{"id":"benjamin_463","name":"Benjamin","also":"Ben-oni","summary":"The younger son of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 35:18). His birth took place at Ephrath, on the road between Bethel and Bethlehem, at a short distance from the latter place.","verses":157,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[12]},{"id":"joseph_1710","name":"Joseph","also":"Zaphnath-paaneah","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Jacob by Rachel (Gen. 30:23, 24), who, on the occasion of his birth, said, “God hath taken away [Heb. ‘asaph] my reproach.”","verses":199,"father":"Israel","mother":"Rachel","v":[13,16]},{"id":"ephraim_1206","name":"Ephraim","also":"","summary":"Double fruitfulness (“for God had made him fruitful in the land of his affliction”). The second son of Joseph, born in Egypt (Gen. 41:52; 46:20).","verses":160,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[17]},{"id":"manasseh_1928","name":"Manasseh","also":"Manasses","summary":"The elder of the two sons of Joseph. He and his brother Ephraim were afterwards adopted by Jacob as his own sons (48:1).","verses":109,"father":"Joseph","mother":"Asenath","v":[17]},{"id":"zebulun_3002","name":"Zebulun","also":"Zabulon","summary":"Dwelling, the sixth and youngest son of Jacob and Leah (Gen. 30:20). Little is known of his personal history.","verses":46,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[18]},{"id":"issachar_645","name":"Issachar","also":"","summary":"Hired (Gen. 30:18). “God hath given me,” said Leah, “my hire (Heb. sekhari)...and she called his name Issachar.” He was Jacob’s ninth son, and was born in Padan-aram (comp. 28:2).","verses":38,"father":"Israel","mother":"Leah","v":[18]},{"id":"gad_1262","name":"Gad","also":"","summary":"Jacob’s seventh son, by Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid, and the brother of Asher (Gen. 30:11-13; 46:16, 18).","verses":55,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[20]},{"id":"dan_973","name":"Dan","also":"","summary":"The fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s maid (Gen. 30:6, “God hath judged me”, Heb. dananni).","verses":63,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[22]},{"id":"naphtali_2149","name":"Naphtali","also":"Nephthalim","summary":"My wrestling, the fifth son of Jacob. His mother was Bilhah, Rachel’s handmaid (Gen. 30:8). When Jacob went down into Egypt, Naphtali had four sons (Gen. 46:24).","verses":49,"father":"Israel","mother":"Bilhah","v":[23]},{"id":"asher_337","name":"Asher","also":"Aser","summary":"Happy, Jacob’s eigth son; his mother was Zilpah, Leah’s handmaid (Gen. 30:13). Of the tribe founded by him nothing is recorded beyond its holding a place in the list of the tribes (35:26; 46:17; Ex. 1:4, etc.) It increased in numbers twenty-nine percent, during the thirty-eight years’ wanderings.","verses":43,"father":"Israel","mother":"Zilpah","v":[24]}],"places":[{"id":"mount_paran_850","name":"mount Paran","kind":"Mountain","lat":29.15167,"lon":33.54194,"summary":"Probably the hilly region or upland wilderness on the north of the desert of Paran forming the southern boundary of the Promised Land (Deut. 33:2; Hab. 3:3).","verses":2,"v":[2]},{"id":"seir_1042","name":"Seir","kind":"Region","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"The name of a mountainous region occupied by the Edomites, extending along the eastern side of the Arabah from the south-eastern extremity of the Dead Sea to near the Akabah, or the eastern branch of the Red Sea.","verses":24,"v":[2]},{"id":"sinai_1098","name":"Sinai","kind":"Region","lat":29.5,"lon":34.0,"summary":"Of Sin (the moon god), called also Horeb, the name of the mountain district which was reached by the Hebrews in the third month after the Exodus.","verses":18,"v":[2]},{"id":"massah_771","name":"Massah","kind":"","lat":28.73106,"lon":33.8417,"summary":"Trial, temptation, a name given to the place where the Israelites, by their murmuring for want of water, provoked Jehovah to anger against them.","verses":4,"v":[8]},{"id":"meribah_783","name":"Meribah","kind":"Landmark (Spring)","lat":28.73106,"lon":33.8417,"summary":"One of the names given by Moses to the fountain in the desert of Sin, near Rephidim, which issued from the rock in Horeb, which he smote by the divine command, “because of the chiding of the children of Israel” (Ex. 17:1-7).","verses":2,"v":[8]},{"id":"ephraim-territory_1292","name":"Ephraim (Territory)","kind":"Region","lat":32.01632,"lon":35.23283,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1270 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":15,"v":[17]},{"id":"west-manasseh_1291","name":"West Manasseh","kind":"Region","lat":32.48192,"lon":35.31006,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1269 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":19,"v":[17]},{"id":"bashan_159","name":"Bashan","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Light soil, first mentioned in Gen. 14:5, where it is said that Chedorlaomer and his confederates “smote the Rephaim in Ashteroth,” where Og the king of Bashan had his residence.","verses":52,"v":[22]},{"id":"asher_1287","name":"Asher","kind":"Region","lat":32.91454,"lon":35.15813,"summary":"Added from Digital Manna places-1264 (LPF sync 2026-10-13)","verses":20,"v":[24,25]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[2063,1293,1293,1293,834,4872,376,376,430,430,1288,1121,1121,1121,6440,4194,4194],[559,559,3068,3068,935,5514,5514,2224,2224,0,0,8165,8165,3313,3313,3313,2022,2022,6290,857,857,7233,7233,6944,6944,6944,799,799,799,3225,3225,3225,3225],[637,2245,2245,5971,5971,3605,6918,6918,6918,6918,3027,3027,3027,1992,1992,8497,8497,7272,7272,7272,5375,5375,1703,1703],[8451,8451,4872,4872,6680,0,4181,4181,6952,6952,6952,3290,3290],[1961,1961,1961,1961,4428,3484,3484,7218,7218,7218,5971,5971,5971,622,7626,7626,7626,3478,3478,3162,3162],[7205,7205,2421,408,408,4191,1961,4962,4962,4557,4557],[2063,3063,3063,559,559,3068,3068,8085,6963,6963,3063,3063,935,935,935,413,5971,5971,3027,3027,3027,3027,7378,7378,7378,7378,1961,1961,1961,1961,5828,5828,6862,6862,6862],[3878,3878,559,559,8550,8550,8550,8550,8550,224,224,224,2623,2623,2623,376,834,5254,5254,4532,4532,7378,7378,5921,4325,4325,4809,4809],[559,559,1,1,1,517,517,3808,3808,3808,7200,7200,3808,3808,251,251,3808,3808,3808,3045,1121,1121,1121,3588,8104,8104,565,565,5341,5341,1285,1285],[3384,3384,3384,4941,4941,3290,3290,8451,8451,8451,3478,3478,7760,7760,7760,6988,639,639,3632,3632,3632,3632,5921,4196,4196],[1288,2428,2428,3068,3068,7521,7521,6467,6467,3027,3027,3027,4272,4975,4975,6965,6965,6965,6965,6965,6965,8130,8130,8130,8130,4480,4480,4480,6965,6965,6965],[1144,1144,559,559,3039,3039,3039,3068,3068,3068,7931,983,5921,5921,2653,2653,5921,3605,3117,3117,3802,3802,3802,3802,7931,7931],[3130,3130,559,559,776,776,776,1288,1288,3068,3068,3068,4022,4022,4022,2919,8064,8064,80